# windows only, layered over shared/prefs/org.eclipse.ui.workbench.prefs
# Geist Mono's Nerd Font build for the plain and C editors and the Terminal, the font every editor and
# terminal uses, so the prompt's symbols draw. the short font string has no platform part; 14 points
# here matches the Mac's 18 on screen, since points are larger. the Terminal uses the Mono build, whose icons fill one cell
# windows looks fonts up by their GDI family name, which Nerd Fonts shortens to GeistMono NF and
# GeistMono NFM. the long names that macOS and Linux use resolve to Arial here
org.eclipse.jface.textfont=1|GeistMono NF|14.0|0|
org.eclipse.cdt.ui.editors.textfont=1|GeistMono NF|14.0|0|
terminal.views.view.font.definition=1|GeistMono NFM|14.0|0|
